            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Moral and Social Reforms</strong><br>\nSolon is also known for his moral and social reforms, which were aimed at creating a more cohesive society. He legislated against political corruption and encouraged fair trade practices. Solon's laws also included measures to promote social harmony, such as forbidding extravagant displays of wealth and public mourning.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Solon's Poetry</strong><br>\nAs a poet, Solon used his verses to express his political and social ideals. His poems served as a medium to communicate his reforms and to educate the Athenian public about his vision for a just and balanced society. Some of his poetry has survived, offering insight into his thinking and the society of his time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Solon</strong><br>\nAfter completing his reforms, Solon left Athens to travel for ten years, allowing his laws to take root without his influence. His reforms did not solve all of Athens' problems, but they were a significant first step towards democracy. Solon's work as a lawmaker and his fair and balanced approach to governance earned him a lasting place as one of the Seven Sages of Greece.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
